{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# S3 (a8ea): Config-driven type mapping + type-granular skip\n\n## Context / Problem\nEpic 3d7a adds a config-driven mapping seam (S1: `mapping_config.MappingLayer` with a\n`type_map` axis, `SKIP=\"skip\"`, `resolve_for_project`, `validate`). S2 made STATUS\nconfig-driven — the template: `config.effective_status_map` (`config.py:77`) threads a\nper-project `status_map` through the Backend port into the field mappers; `rebar-status:`\nstamp in `outbound_labels.py`; reverse-map-free inbound `recover_status_label` (`:152`). TYPE\nis hard-coded: `LOCAL_TYPE_TO_JIRA` (`adapters/jira_family/value_maps.py:40` =\n`{bug,story,task,epic}`), `EXCLUDED_SYNC_TYPES` (`config.py:13`). Distinct types can collapse\nto one Jira type (lossy). Syncable = `get_args(TicketType)` (`types.py:23`) −\n`EXCLUDED_SYNC_TYPES` = `{bug,epic,story,task}`. S3 is type-only.\n\n## Approach\nThree outcomes for `ticket_type`: **remap** (effective type map), **skip** (per-project via\nSKIP), **FAIL-CLOSED** on an undecided syncable type. Round-trip safety: NEW `rebar-type:`\nannotation label symmetric with `rebar-status:`, reverse-map-free inbound. Type resolution +\nfail-closed live in TWO upstream places — the up-front gate and the mapper. acli is UNTOUCHED.\n\n### Finding — acli.create_issue stays a passthrough (NO rewrite)\nOn the differ path acli NEVER sees a raw local type: the mapper\n(`outbound_fields._map_local_to_jira_fields:143`, DC `jira_datacenter/backend.py:86`) already\nsets `issuetype` to the mapped Jira NAME, and `dispatch_one.py:188-195` derives\n`ticket_data[\"ticket_type\"]` FROM that name. Re-resolving via `LOCAL_TYPE_TO_JIRA` inside acli\nwould fail-close on EVERY differ create (`\"Story\"` isn't a key). ALL `client.create_issue`\ncallers: `dispatch_one.py:209` and `apply_outbound.py:101` pass mapper output;\n`access_check.py:150` passes a FIXED probe `{\"ticket_type\":\"task\"}` relying on `.capitalize()`.\nNone pass a config-mappable raw local type, so `acli.py:282` is CORRECT and unchanged.\n\n### Finding 1 (G7) — fail-closed fires ONCE UP-FRONT, before the mutation loop\nParent AC (\"load-time fail-closed on undecided types\") is PRIMARY. `effective_status_map` is\ninvoked LAZILY per-ticket in the differ loop, so a per-ticket gate would NOT fire before\nmutations. FIX:\n- NEW `config.effective_type_map(project_key, root)` mirrors `effective_status_map` (`:77`):\n  `builtin=MappingLayer(type_map=LOCAL_TYPE_TO_JIRA)` ← `resolve_for_project`; returns\n  `{k:v for k,v in resolved.type_map.items() if v != SKIP}`.\n- NEW `config.assert_type_decisions_complete(project_key, root)`: every syncable type\n  (`get_args(TicketType) − EXCLUDED_SYNC_TYPES`) must be DECIDED — target OR `SKIP` — else\n  raise `MappingConfigError` (guards a future TicketType; built-in covers all four today).\n- WIRING (proves fail-closed-before-mutation): call it ONCE at the top of\n  `compute_outbound_mutations` (`outbound_differ.py:298`) — after config load `:377`, BEFORE\n  `_compute_outbound_select_absent_gets` (`:381`) and the per-ticket loop (`:430`) — over the\n  DISTINCT project keys of `local_tickets` (via `projects_store.resolve_project`). (S1's\n  `validate` stays uncalled — S4.)\n\n### Finding 3 (E2) — where the per-project excluded set comes from (SKIP entries)\nNEW `config.effective_excluded_sync_types(project_key, root)` = `EXCLUDED_SYNC_TYPES` UNION\n`{k for k,v in resolved.type_map.items() if v == mapping_config.SKIP}`, over the SAME\n`resolve_for_project` layer `effective_type_map` uses. Reuses S1's SKIP sentinel\n(`mapping_config.py:51`) as the type-granular skip signal — no separate axis. A local type\nmapped to `SKIP` is excluded for that project ON TOP of the built-in set.\n\n### Finding — reverse TYPE map for the lossy-stamp rule (G6)\n`_desired_type_annotation` stamps only when the forward target does NOT reverse to this local\ntype — needs a Jira→local reverse map. `config.py` has none, and `outbound_labels.py` imports\nONLY `config`. FIX: NEW `config.jira_to_local_type` mirroring `jira_to_local_status` (`:64`),\nlock-stepped with `inbound_fields._JIRA_TO_LOCAL_TYPE` (`:105`) via a parity test.\n\n### Finding 4 (G1G2) — thread type_map through ALL THREE OutboundMapper impls\n`type_map` must follow every one of S2's THREE `map_local_to_remote` bodies + the shared field\nmappers, or the differ's `type_map=` kwarg hits a signature lacking it → `TypeError`. Add\n`type_map: dict[str,str] | None = None` (beside `status_map`) to: (1) `OutboundMapper` Protocol\n(`_backend.py:372`); (2) Cloud `JiraBackend.map_local_to_remote` (`jira/backend.py:73`, forwards\n`status_map` `:89`); (3) DC (`jira_datacenter/backend.py:121`) — each forwards into its field\nmapper. Then (4) `outbound_fields._map_local_to_jira_fields` (`:101`) resolves issuetype via\n`type_map` (replacing coerce `:143`), fail-closed; (5) DC `_map_local_to_dc_fields` (coerce\n`:86`) same. NEW `outbound_differ._effective_type_map_for` mirrors `_effective_status_map_for`\n(`:272`); `_compute_outbound_create_mutation` (`outbound_mutation_builders.py:37`) passes it.\n\n## Surface-parity census — stamp + inbound + prefix filters\n- Stamp: NEW `outbound_labels._REBAR_TYPE_LABEL_PREFIX=\"rebar-type:\"`,\n  `_desired_type_annotation` (mirror `:89`, using `config.jira_to_local_type`),\n  `_diff_type_annotation_labels` (mirror `:114`). Threaded at BOTH\n  `outbound_mutation_builders.py` sites: create `:81`/`:138`; update `:276`/`:281`.\n- Inbound: NEW `inbound_fields.recover_type_label` (mirror `recover_status_label` `:152`) +\n  `_LOCAL_TYPE_VOCAB` from `get_args(TicketType)`; wired at `:311-313`, label-over-raw `:326`.\n- Per-project excluded set replaces the single `EXCLUDED_SYNC_TYPES` read (`:377`) at BOTH\n  consumers: `:430` (loop) and `:519` (`_compute_outbound_select_absent_gets`).\n- `rebar-type:` added to ALL FOUR prefix tuples: `outbound_labels.py:34` (re-export\n  `outbound_differ.py:77`); `inbound_collection_diffs.py:88` (re-export\n  `inbound_differ.py:31`; read by `reconcile_check.py:96`); `differ.py:105`\n  `_BRIDGE_INTERNAL_LABEL_PREFIXES`; `inbound_translate.py:58` `_BRIDGE_INTERNAL_TAG_PREFIXES`\n  (keeps its `imported:` omission).\n\n## Scope\nNew/changed: `config.py` (effective_type_map, assert_type_decisions_complete,\neffective_excluded_sync_types, jira_to_local_type); type_map signature thread through\n`_backend.py:372` + all three OutboundMapper impls + both field mappers (Finding 4);\n`outbound_labels.py`, `outbound_mutation_builders.py`, `outbound_differ.py`, `inbound_fields.py`,\n`inbound_collection_diffs.py`, `differ.py`, `inbound_translate.py` (census).\n**acli.py is NOT modified.** All additions small; module-size cap 800 LOC (target 200-500).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n(`tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_type_mapping.py`)\n- [ ] `test_fail_closed_fires_before_mutation_loop` — undecided syncable type raises\n  `MappingConfigError` from `compute_outbound_mutations` before any mutation is built.\n- [ ] `test_skip_is_a_valid_type_decision` — a `SKIP` type passes the gate, is in\n  `effective_excluded_sync_types`, absent from `effective_type_map`.\n- [ ] `test_effective_type_map_default_equals_builtin` — no `[mapping]` ⇒ built-in; project\n  `type_map` remaps.\n- [ ] `test_effective_excluded_union_builtin_and_skip` — == `EXCLUDED_SYNC_TYPES` ∪ SKIP keys.\n- [ ] `test_type_skip_excludes_ticket_both_consumers` — excluded at `:430` AND `:519`.\n- [ ] `test_type_map_threaded_through_all_three_mappers` — `type_map=` reaches all impls, no\n  `TypeError`.\n- [ ] `test_rebar_type_label_stamped_when_lossy` — collapsing types stamp `rebar-type:` at\n  create + update via `config.jira_to_local_type`.\n- [ ] `test_rebar_type_label_recovered_reverse_map_free` — `recover_type_label` restores it.\n- [ ] `test_rebar_type_prefix_excluded_all_four_tuples` — filtered by all four tuples.\n- [ ] `test_jira_to_local_type_parity` — == `inbound_fields._JIRA_TO_LOCAL_TYPE`.\n- [ ] `test_local_type_vocab_derived_from_ticket_type` — == `get_args(TicketType)`.\n\nTest tier: unit"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787358192934073001,"uuid":"60be9915-fda7-4469-aa2e-081d894cbfe5"}